## What changed

**`prereg-budget-aware.md` — full rewrite.** §1.1 states why *no* behavioural experiment can falsify `PAPER.md` §5 (the "neither" quantifies over cap and tokenizer; both are near-analytic as operationalised). §1.2 reframes E2 as a test of limitation (i) and a **scope condition on §5's triage heuristic**. Every falsification claim removed. New §15 tracks all seven review §4 errors plus an eighth (NATIVE-only censoring table under a two-arm rule 8).

**Decoupled-announcement block.** `max_tokens = 2048`, announced ∈ {128, 256, 2048}. Headline estimand is now a *within-AWARE dose contrast* — the two prompts differ only in the integer, so PLACEBO's nuisance channel cancels exactly. Family: **5 cells, both arms** (Qwen NATIVE de/th + TRANSLATE-ACT de/th/sw; NATIVE-sw excluded at 11.35% censoring), Holm α₁ = **0.01**. Manipulation check is now diagnostic: R1 predicts p50 ≈ 128, R2 predicts the unchanged BLIND median (250–378), separation 122–250 tokens; gate = ≥30% median drop in ≥4/5 cells.

**Language-neutral TAG** condition (`TOKEN_BUDGET: {budget}`), Δ 10–11 tokens in all six cells, needs no PLACEBO (within-condition contrast), and is the pre-stated fallback if translations fail verification.

**MDE/power table** (`src/e2_power.py` + script + 20 tests → `analysis-out/e2_power.{json,md}`), split-half null calibrated against E1's published SEs: 0.897/1.194/0.999 vs 0.824/1.207/1.107.

